# What the code-knowledge graph should not index.
#
# graphify already skips node_modules/, target/, out/, build/, dist/ and
# .gitignore'd paths on its own (detect._SKIP_DIRS). This file covers what it
# cannot infer: vendored dependencies that are tracked here as git submodules,
# and generated analysis output that looks like source.
#
# The point is signal. Indexing forge's dependency tree buries 363 first-party
# contracts under 1,864 vendored ones, and every community the clusterer finds
# turns out to be "OpenZeppelin".

# Forge dependencies — git submodules, so neither .gitignore nor _SKIP_DIRS
# catches them. Inherited OpenZeppelin/solmate/LayerZero symbols still appear
# in the graph as external reference nodes.
evm/lib/

# Vendored Rust (rust-lightning and friends) under the LN workspace — the old
# graphify-out indexed this wholesale, which is what made it noise.
quid-ln/lib/

# Generated analysis artefacts, not source.
evm/slither-out/
evm/noir/passport-vks/
evm/noir/**/target/

# Stale output of the previous, Rust-only run. Superseded by SPV/graphify-out.
quid-ln/graphify-out/
